import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.LangDefs
import Submission.NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.auxFieldHypExists
import Submission.NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.kernelLeOfAuxFieldHyp

/-!
# Lang, ANT, Chapter X §2, Theorem 2 (kernel containment), via Artin's lemma

This module proves the requested statement
`NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.kernelLeOfAdmissibleViaArtinLemma`: for a finite cyclic
extension `L/K` of number fields, an admissible modulus `m > 0` divisible by all the primes
ramified in `L/K`, every fractional ideal `A` of `K` coprime to `(m)` with trivial ideal-theoretic
Artin symbol lies in the subgroup generated by the principal ray `P(m) = principalRay K m` and the
norm ray `\mathfrak{N}(m) = normRay K L m`.

The proof is the classical one of Lang (*Algebraic Number Theory*, Ch. X §2, Theorem 2) /
Childress (*Class Field Theory*, Prop. 2.2), split into the two halves that are proved in the
sibling modules:

* **Artin's auxiliary field** (Lang's "Artin's lemma", van der Waerden's elementary lemmas):
  `NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.auxFieldHypExists`
  (`Submission/Work/CFTLib/ArtinReciprocityIdeal/auxFieldHypExists.lean`, axiom-clean) provides,
  for the finite set of primes occurring in the factorisation of `A`, a modulus `M` and, inside
  `L(ζ_M)`, a field `E` with `E ∩ L = K` together with subfields `E_𝔭 ≤ E` such that
  `E_𝔭·ℚ(ζ_M) = L(ζ_M)` and `𝔭` splits completely in `E_𝔭/K`
  (this is the *corrected* Artin-lemma interface `NK.CFTLib.ARL.AuxFieldHyp`, since the naive
  single-field form is false for two primes of equal norm — see
  `Submission/Work/CFTLib/Existence/AuxFieldCorrected.lean`);

* **the transfer** (Childress, *CFT*, Prop. 2.2): `NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.kernelLeOfAuxFieldHyp`
  (`Submission/Work/CFTLib/ArtinReciprocityIdeal/kernelLeOfAuxFieldHyp.lean`, axiom-clean) turns the
  auxiliary fields into the containment `ker Ψ ⊆ P(m)·𝔑(m)`, using the cyclotomic case of the
  reciprocity law for the cells `L·E_𝔭/E_𝔭 ⊆ E_𝔭(ζ_M)/E_𝔭`
  (`NK.CFTLib.ARL.cyclotomicCellKernelLe_B`), the norm/restriction compatibility of the Artin
  symbol (`NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.artinSym_restrict_relNorm`), the transitivity of the
  relative ideal norm (`NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.relNormUnit_trans`) and the norm descent
  of the principal ray (`NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.norm_principalRay_le`).

Note that the admissibility hypothesis `hadm` is not needed for the containment itself (the
transfer produces it at every modulus containing the ramified primes); it is part of the statement
because it is what makes the containment equivalent to the product condition
`artinKillsPrincipal K L m` via the index inequalities. -/

set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

namespace NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal

theorem kernelLeOfAdmissibleViaArtinLemma (K L : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field L]
    [NumberField L] [Algebra K L] [FiniteDimensional K L] [IsGalois K L]
    [IsCyclic (Gal(L/K))] [IsMulCommutative (Gal(L/K))] (m : ℕ) (hm : 0 < m)
    (hadm : NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.IsAdmissible K L m)
    (hram : ∀ p : NK.Chebotarev.PrimeIdeal K,
      ¬ NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.IsUnramified (K := K) (L := L) p →
      (m : NumberField.RingOfIntegers K) ∈ p.asIdeal) :
    ∀ A : NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.Frac K,
      NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.FracCoprime m A →
      NK.CFTLib.Arl.artinSym (K := K) (L := L)
        (fun a b : Gal(L/K) => IsMulCommutative.is_comm.comm a b) A = 1 →
      A ∈ NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.principalRay K m ⊔
          NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.normRay K L m :=
  NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.kernelLeOfAuxFieldHyp K L m hm
    (NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.auxFieldHypExists K L m hm) hram

end NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal
